I read the failing bar, then traced the two paths that produce hand entries:    
flag_calls() (which evaluator_history() calls for a model evaluator) and the    
assembly block that turns hand into either a hand-time refusal or an allowance. 
The seam the bar draws is where the value came from: a typed/ledger value       
(inputs-no-ledger, ledger-hand, ledger-no-writer) is what the switch admits; a  
value the reader synthesised from the response Date header or created epoch     
(server-header, response-created) is a model evaluator's check time with no     
logger source, and the switch must not admit it. So the fix is: have            
flag_calls() report the entries it added, keep the evaluator's unstamped entries
separately, and refuse them with kind time only when the switch is on (the      
no-switch path keeps its existing hand-time refusal, unchanged), naming the log 
and every call it did not stamp.                                                

