The failed block can't match because the in-function --allow-hand-times refusal 
I proposed earlier is already in evaluator_history, sitting between the two     
lines the block was replacing. That leaves the file inconsistent: block 3 made  
evaluator_history return "unsourced": unsourced and blocks 4–6 made build()     
refuse ev_unsourced, but unsourced is never assigned — so the module would raise
NameError at run time, and once fixed the same entries would be refused twice   
(once here, once at the assembly point).                                        

The fix is to define unsourced where flag_calls() is called, and drop the       
duplicate refusal inside evaluator_history — build() already refuses those      
entries under the switch, beside the no-switch hand-time refusal, so the switch 
is decided in one place and each entry is named once.                           

